via checksum before and after. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured a healthy baseline (boot_id, permissions, checksums), issued a native reboot, polled through the outage, confirmed a new boot_id after recovery, and re-verified ownership, permissions, and data checksums plus persistence of the new user/group post-restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected /srv/inventory contents and existing ownership on node1\",\"Checked for pre-existing inventorysvc user and inventory-readers group (neither existed)\",\"Created group inventory-readers and system user inventorysvc via sudo -n\",\"Recursively chowned /srv/inventory to inventorysvc:inventory-readers\",\"Set directories to 750 and files to 640 via sudo -n find ... chmod\",\"Verified final permissions and confirmed file contents unchanged (records.csv, config.json)\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime -s, ownership/permission listing, sha256 checksums of data files\",\"Triggered a native reboot on node1 via backgrounded sudo -n reboot so the ack returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed from 4ebdfa06-... to 9e1e5dce-... proving an actual restart\",\"Re-verified post-restart ownership/permissions, data checksums, and persistence of inventorysvc user and inventory-readers group\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Existing /srv/inventory data ownership repaired to inventorysvc:inventory-readers with correct access (owner full, group read, others none), contents preserved\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2cb45c4a895a4977\",\"cmd-8bf2eef03bdb4125\"],\"summary\":\"Initial inspection showed root:root ownership and no inventorysvc user or inventory-readers group. After creating both and applying chown -R + chmod (750 dirs / 640 files), verification listing shows inventorysvc:inventory-readers ownership with 750/640 modes, and cat of records.csv/config.json shows original data intact.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 healthy baseline captured before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-277f2ce8f1bd49f1\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 4ebdfa06-919e-48a9-8a15-475d9007662c, uptime -s, permission listing (inventorysvc:inventory-readers 750/640), and sha256 checksums of records.csv and config.json prior to reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0721fbe78bb2492b\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sleep 2; sudo -n reboot' via setsid so the exec call returned 'reboot scheduled' immediately, before the node went down.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart proven via changed boot identity, then recovery polled\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-eb701e497d444d8f\",\"cmd-c73284a8ac624021\",\"cmd-e77c58024857408d\",\"cmd-2a7d668fa06e453d\",\"cmd-cfd014a6655b4eb6\"],\"summary\":\"First poll still showed old boot_id (reboot not yet triggered); next two polls timed out/connection-reset confirming the node was down; final poll succeeded with new boot_id 9e1e5dce-2b48-4610-a68e-dbe3e1b2c60e, proving an actual restart occurred (not just elapsed time).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 post-restart recovery of required state (ownership, permissions, data integrity, user/group persistence)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c23d2d41bee24c4a\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart check shows /srv/inventory still owned inventorysvc:inventory-readers with 750/640 modes, sha256 checksums of both data files unchanged from baseline, and getent confirms inventorysvc user and inventory-readers group persisted across reboot.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Repaired /srv/inventory on node1: created system user inventorysvc and group inventory-readers (neither existed), chowned the tree recursively to inventorysvc:inventory-readers, and set mode 750 on directories / 640 on files so the owner has full access, the group can read, and other users have no access. Existing data (records.csv, config.json) was preserved and verified byte-identical via checksum before and after. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured a healthy baseline (boot_id, permissions, checksums), issued a native reboot, polled through the outage, confirmed a new boot_id after recovery, and re-verified ownership, permissions, and data checksums plus persistence of the new user/group post-restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected /srv/inventory contents and existing ownership on node1","Checked for pre-existing inventorysvc user and inventory-readers group (neither existed)","Created group inventory-readers and system user inventorysvc via sudo -n","Recursively chowned /srv/inventory to inventorysvc:inventory-readers","Set directories to 750 and files to 640 via sudo -n find ... chmod","Verified final permissions and confirmed file contents unchanged (records.csv, config.json)","Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime -s, ownership/permission listing, sha256 checksums of data files","Triggered a native reboot on node1 via backgrounded sudo -n reboot so the ack returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned","Confirmed boot_id changed from 4ebdfa06-... to 9e1e5dce-... proving an actual restart","Re-verified post-restart ownership/permissions, data checksums, and persistence of inventorysvc user and inventory-readers group"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Existing /srv/inventory data ownership repaired to inventorysvc:inventory-readers with correct access (owner full, group read, others none), contents preserved","command_ids":["cmd-2cb45c4a895a4977","cmd-8bf2eef03bdb4125"],"summary":"Initial inspection showed root:root ownership and no inventorysvc user or inventory-readers group. After creating both and applying chown -R + chmod (750 dirs / 640 files), verification listing shows inventorysvc:inventory-readers ownership with 750/640 modes, and cat of records.csv/config.json shows original data intact."},{"requirement":"Node1 healthy baseline captured before restart","command_ids":["cmd-277f2ce8f1bd49f1"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 4ebdfa06-919e-48a9-8a15-475d9007662c, uptime -s, permission listing (inventorysvc:inventory-readers 750/640), and sha256 checksums of records.csv and config.json prior to reboot."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-0721fbe78bb2492b"],"summary":"Backgrounded 'sleep 2; sudo -n reboot' via setsid so the exec call returned 'reboot scheduled' immediately, before the node went down."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart proven via changed boot identity, then recovery polled","command_ids":["cmd-eb701e497d444d8f","cmd-c73284a8ac624021","cmd-e77c58024857408d","cmd-2a7d668fa06e453d","cmd-cfd014a6655b4eb6"],"summary":"First poll still showed old boot_id (reboot not yet triggered); next two polls timed out/connection-reset confirming the node was down; final poll succeeded with new boot_id 9e1e5dce-2b48-4610-a68e-dbe3e1b2c60e, proving an actual restart occurred (not just elapsed time)."},{"requirement":"Node1 post-restart recovery of required state (ownership, permissions, data integrity, user/group persistence)","command_ids":["cmd-c23d2d41bee24c4a"],"summary":"Post-restart check shows /srv/inventory still owned inventorysvc:inventory-readers with 750/640 modes, sha256 checksums of both data files unchanged from baseline, and getent confirms inventorysvc user and inventory-readers group persisted across reboot."}]},"ttft_ms":1658,"type":"result","duration_ms":46082,"uuid":"fd5956b4-c22b-4507-b354-679713f74e9f","ttft_stream_ms":801,"time_to_request_ms":68,"first_content_frame_ms":801,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
